## Implementation status

`agentix-qwen` is now a workspace member. It uses pure-Rust dependencies for
tokenization/template rendering (`tokenizers` with default features disabled and
`fancy-regex`, `minijinja`, `serde_json`); no native deps were added by them.
The initial saved ngram/budget/rows modules have been formatted; new reference.rs
implements FP32 top-k routing, grouped offset RMS norm, direct-weight sigmoid-gated
RMS norm, and a single-value-head GatedDeltaNet recurrence. Recurrent updates commit
only after shape/numeric checks succeed. This is NOT a complete layer/decoder.

Ten integration tests cover independent BigInt-derived n-gram vectors, EOS/chunks,
snapshot/restore and rejection atomicity, analytical routing/norm/recurrence cases,
row offsets/LRU/cache bounds/truncation and independent RAM/VRAM checked admission.
The row store requires an independently validated decoder and immutable model data;
it is not a GGUF loader. Blocking I/O must remain outside Tokio workers.

Nix `packages.agentix-qwen` runs tests and installs the rlib plus provenance.
Updated workspace manifests/stubs in perSystem/packages.nix. Cargo.lock includes
the workspace member and tokenizer/template dependencies. New quickstart.md
explains foundation commands and limitations.
T031–T033 marked complete at CPU-foundation scope.

Validation so far:
- `nix develop --command cargo fmt -p agentix-qwen`: completed.
- `nix develop --command cargo test -p agentix-qwen`: all 10 passed.
- `nix build .#agentix-qwen --no-link`: passed, including 10 release-mode tests.
- Format check and Clippy passed after three mechanical is_multiple_of lint fixes.
  Crate tests and Nix build passed again. Workspace tests now pass; see below.
- First dev shell failed because the new member was not yet in Nix manifest/stub
  lists; fixed those lists and retried the same workflow successfully.
- No complete Qwen fixture, GPU, Qwen daemon integration, full-model
  inference or throughput measurements. Do not mark T006–T030 complete.

